---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How we work — Blackbook Racing"
  description="Methodology and ledger. UK flat racing — turf and all-weather — with a hurdle add-on for Blackbook members. Pre-off timestamps, reconciled to Betfair SP."
>
  <article class="page">
    <p class="eyebrow">How we work</p>
    <h1 class="page-title">Methodology &amp; ledger</h1>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>The focus</h2>
      <p>
        Blackbook Racing is a UK flat-racing service — turf and all-weather. Every race day we
        publish a slate of pre-off selections, post them to Telegram and to the public ledger, and
        reconcile every result to Betfair Starting Price after the race. Blackbook-tier members
        also get our hurdle add-on, plus a curated list of horses worth tracking through the
        season.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>What we do each morning</h2>
      <p>
        Every morning of UK racing, every runner in every UK flat (and hurdle, for Blackbook) race
        goes through our methodology. A selection only fires when a runner clears the threshold on
        a stream we've validated across years of historical data. The team reviews the day's slate
        before it goes out. Selections are timestamped pre-off. Results reconcile to Betfair SP
        after the race.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>The methodology</h2>
      <p>
        We assess every runner across a deep stack of signals — speed figures, handicap context,
        market behaviour, trainer and jockey form, and our own private indicators built on decades
        of UK racing data. The output is a layered slate. The single highest-conviction pick each
        race day is the Free tier. The widest slate — the full top-conviction layer, plus value
        picks, form picks, hurdles, the seasonal blackbook, drift alerts and weekly editorial — is
        Blackbook.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>How we measure ourselves</h2>
      <p>
        Headline performance is fully public — aggregate ROI, strike rate, and per-tier breakdowns
        by race code and signal type, all reconciled to Betfair SP. The full pick-by-pick audit
        trail (winners and losers, with prices, timestamps and reasoning) lives in the members
        area. Timestamps are pre-off. No retroactive edits.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>What we don't do</h2>
      <p>
        Claim guaranteed returns. Post stakes after the result. Hide losing days. Pool funds or
        accept stakes on anyone's behalf. Sell systems we wouldn't bet ourselves.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>The Blackbook</h2>
      <p>
        Blackbook-tier members get our curated list of horses worth tracking — animals we've
        flagged across multiple runs and expect to fire when conditions align. Each entry has a
        reason and a target run window. Updated through the season, with weekly editorial
        commentary on what's working, what's not, and what we're watching next.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>

  <style>
    .page {
      padding-top: 16px;
    }

    .eyebrow {
      font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
      font-size: 11px;
      letter-spacing: 0.25em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--gold);
      font-weight: 600;
      text-align: center;
      margin-bottom: 12px;
    }

    .page-title {
      font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond', serif;
      font-weight: 700;
      font-size: 40px;
      letter-spacing: 0.04em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      text-align: center;
      margin-bottom: 56px;
    }

    .block {
      max-width: 680px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding-bottom: 36px;
    }

    .block + .block {
      padding-top: 36px;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    }

    .block h2 {
      font-size: 20px;
      letter-spacing: 0.1em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      font-weight: 600;
      margin-bottom: 14px;
    }

    .block p {
      font-family: 'EB Garamond', serif;
      font-size: 19px;
      line-height: 1.6;
      color: var(--ink);
    }

    @media (max-width: 640px) {
      .page-title {
        font-size: 28px;
        margin-bottom: 40px;
      }

      .block h2 {
        font-size: 17px;
      }

      .block p {
        font-size: 17px;
      }
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
